    "tool_calls": 33,
    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package to satisfy all acceptance criteria. The bugs found and fixed were:\n\n1. **varint.py**: `decode_uvarint` only read a single byte instead of properly decoding multi-byte LEB128. Fixed to loop until a byte with MSB=0 is found, accumulating 7-bit groups.\n\n2. **header.py**: Record count was packed/unpacked as big-endian (`>I`) but the actual format uses little-endian (`<I`). Fixed both `pack_header` and `parse_header`.\n\n3. **crc.py**: `compute_crc` was missing the final XOR with 0xFFFFFFFF, producing non-standard CRC-32 values. Added the final XOR to produce standard IEEE CRC-32. Also added `update_crc` and `finalize_crc` helpers for incremental/streaming CRC computation. Fixed `unpack_crc` to raise `WFormatError(\"truncated\")` instead of `ValueError`.\n\n4. **codec.py**: Records require 4-byte alignment padding (pad raw record size to multiple of ALIGN=4). Added `_pad_to_align()`, updated `encode_record` to append zero-padding, and updated `decode_record` to skip padding",
    "changed_workspace": true
